238. Product of Array Except Self

Given an integer array nums, return an array answer such that answer[i] is equal to the product of all the elements of nums except nums[i].

The product of any prefix or suffix of nums is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit integer.

You must write an algorithm that runs in O(n) time and without using the division operation.

 

Example 1:

Input: nums = [1,2,3,4]
Output: [24,12,8,6]
Example 2:

Input: nums = [-1,1,0,-3,3]
Output: [0,0,9,0,0]
 

Constraints:

2 <= nums.length <= 105
-30 <= nums[i] <= 30
The input is generated such that answer[i] is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit integer.
 

 
Topics
Array
Prefix Sum


Solution:

the solution is to first calculate the product of all the elements in the array 
and then divide the product by each element to get the product of all elements except self.
so the edge cases are only one zero we can append zeros but except zero value 
we can append the product of all non zero values and 
if there are more than one zero we can append all zeros to the result array.

class Solution {
    public int[] productExceptSelf(int[] nums) {
        int arrSum = 1;
        int countZero=0;
        for(int num : nums){
            if(num!=0){
                arrSum*=num;
            }
            if(num==0){
                countZero+=1;
            }
        }
        int[] res= new int[nums.length];
        if(countZero==0){
             for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
                res[i]=arrSum/nums[i];
            }
        }else if(countZero==1){
             for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
                if(nums[i]==0){
                    res[i]=arrSum;
                }else{
                    res[i]=0;
                }
            }
        }else{
            for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
                res[i]=0;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}